Total: 34.5 + 3-5 + 3-4 + 7 = 47.5-50.5 d at the stated bake-off size, and more if it is re-sized.

problems.problem:
At the plan caps, V3 and V4 cannot test their source geometry. Their models are reduced by about 98-99.6%, so they must be re-carded by our own baker, and what remains is mostly our geometry. V4 also uses different species:
- Boxwood for Smaragd;
- Norway maple for sugar maple;
- H. macrophylla for Annabelle.
Judged against photos of the target species, V4 will lose on identity, not realism. The 'gap is geometry' inference does not follow, and V4 cannot serve as the claimed realism ceiling.

problems.evidence:
Maxtree polycounts:
- V122 Thuja occidentalis: 204,508-726,764 polys (paid-libraries research);
- Calamagrostis acutiflora V109: 591,186-1,686,429 per variant (https://maxtree.org/product/plant-models-vol-109/);
- Amelanchier canadensis V183: 115,305-206,526.

Plan caps are clipped evergreen 3k, shrub 3.5k and tree 12k, or 12k/15k/60k raised. For example, 3k from 204k is about a 98.5% cut. The synthesis concedes that 'LOD1 and LOD2 realism comes mostly from our own baking'.

The Megascans seller search on Fab finds no Thuja, and V4 itself says 'there is no Thuja'.

